Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 05:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase-Q-adsense-policy-fix

Google flagged the site for 'Google-served ads on screens without
publisher-content' and low-value content, blocking AdSense approval.

Root cause: GoogleAdsense (Google auto-ads script) was mounted at the
parent and teacher LAYOUT level, so it loaded on every route under
those sections -- including Settings and Messages, which are thin,
navigational/behavioral screens with essentially no unique content.
Auto-ads will place ad units on any page where the script loads,
regardless of whether that page qualifies as publisher-content.

Fix: removed GoogleAdsense from both layouts and mounted it only on
individual pages with substantive, unique content -- dashboards, book
lists, analytics, classroom, challenges, events, progress, book clubs.
Settings and Messages (both parent and teacher) now load no ad script
at all. Kids layout was never affected -- no ads there, unchanged.
